   "source": [
    "# Clustering — Applied on Real Dataset\n",
    "**Mall Customer Segmentation: K-Means, Hierarchical, DBSCAN**\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "## Table of Contents\n",
    "1. Dataset Overview — Mall Customer Data\n",
    "2. EDA — Exploratory Data Analysis\n",
    "3. Feature Engineering & Scaling\n",
    "4. K-Means — Finding Optimal K\n",
    "5. Hierarchical Clustering — Dendrogram\n",
    "6. DBSCAN — Density Based Clustering\n",
    "7. Algorithm Comparison\n",
    "8. Capstone Challenge + Solutions\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 1: Dataset Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "### Keywords:\n",
    "- **Customer Segmentation:** Customers ko similar groups mein divide karna\n",
    "- **RFM Analysis:** Recency, Frequency, Monetary — customer behavior ke 3 dimensions\n",
    "- **Annual Income:** Customer ki yearly salary\n",
    "- **Spending Score:** Mall ne assign kiya 1-100 score based on behavior\n",
    "- **Unsupervised:** Koi pre-defined labels nahi hain"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "\n",
    "# Mall Customer Dataset (inline — no download needed)\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "n = 200\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create realistic customer data\n",
    "data = {\n",
    "    'CustomerID': range(1, n + 1),\n",
    "    'Gender': np.random.choice(['Male', 'Female'], n, p=[0.44, 0.56]),\n",
    "    'Age': np.random.randint(18, 70, n),\n",
    "    'Annual_Income_k': np.concatenate([\n",
    "        np.random.normal(25, 5, 40),   # Low income\n",
    "        np.random.normal(55, 8, 60),   # Mid income\n",
    "        np.random.normal(85, 10, 60),  # High income\n",
    "        np.random.normal(55, 8, 40),   # Mid income\n",
    "    ]).clip(15, 130),\n",
    "    'Spending_Score': np.concatenate([\n",
    "        np.random.normal(45, 8, 40),   # Average spenders (low income)\n",
    "        np.random.normal(25, 7, 60),   # Low spenders (mid income, savers)\n",
    "        np.random.normal(80, 7, 60),   # High spenders (high income)\n",
    "        np.random.normal(70, 8, 40),   # High spenders (mid income)\n",
    "    ]).clip(1, 100)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(data)\n",
    "df['Annual_Income_k'] = df['Annual_Income_k'].round(1)\n",
    "df['Spending_Score'] = df['Spending_Score'].round(1)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Dataset Overview ===\")\n",
    "print(df.head(10).to_string())\n",
    "print(f\"\\nShape: {df.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nNull values: {df.isnull().sum().sum()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 2: EDA — Exploratory Data Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Statistical Summary\n",
    "print(\"=== Statistical Summary ===\")\n",
    "print(df[['Age', 'Annual_Income_k', 'Spending_Score']].describe().round(2))\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(12, 10))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Scatter: Income vs Spending\n",
    "gender_colors = {'Male': 'steelblue', 'Female': 'salmon'}\n",
    "for gender in ['Male', 'Female']:\n",
    "    mask = df['Gender'] == gender\n",
    "    axes[0, 0].scatter(df[mask]['Annual_Income_k'], df[mask]['Spending_Score'],\n",
    "                       c=gender_colors[gender], label=gender, alpha=0.6, s=30)\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_xlabel('Annual Income (k$)')\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_ylabel('Spending Score')\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_title('Income vs Spending Score')\n",
    "axes[0, 0].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Scatter: Age vs Spending\n",
    "axes[0, 1].scatter(df['Age'], df['Spending_Score'], alpha=0.5, c='green', s=30)\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_xlabel('Age')\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_ylabel('Spending Score')\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_title('Age vs Spending Score')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Income distribution\n",
    "axes[1, 0].hist(df['Annual_Income_k'], bins=20, color='steelblue', alpha=0.7, edgecolor='white')\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_xlabel('Annual Income (k$)')\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_title('Income Distribution')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Age distribution\n",
    "axes[1, 1].hist(df['Age'], bins=15, color='coral', alpha=0.7, edgecolor='white')\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_xlabel('Age')\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_title('Age Distribution')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('Mall Customer — EDA', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 3: Feature Engineering & Scaling\n",
    "\n",
    "### Keywords:\n",
    "- **Feature Selection:** Which features to use for clustering\n",
    "- **Scaling:** StandardScaler — mean=0, std=1 (required for distance-based algorithms)\n",
    "- **Encoding:** Gender (Male/Female) → numbers (0/1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# We'll cluster on Income and Spending Score (most business-relevant)\n",
    "X = df[['Annual_Income_k', 'Spending_Score']].values\n",
    "\n",
    "# Scale\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Feature matrix shape: {X.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Before scaling: Income mean={X[:, 0].mean():.1f}, std={X[:, 0].std():.1f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"After scaling:  Income mean={X_scaled[:, 0].mean():.3f}, std={X_scaled[:, 0].std():.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 4: K-Means — Finding Optimal K"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score\n",
    "\n",
    "# Elbow Method + Silhouette Score\n",
    "inertias = []\n",
    "silhouette_scores = []\n",
    "k_range = range(2, 10)\n",
    "\n",
    "for k in k_range:\n",
    "    km = KMeans(n_clusters=k, random_state=42, n_init=10)\n",
    "    km.fit(X_scaled)\n",
    "    inertias.append(km.inertia_)\n",
    "    silhouette_scores.append(silhouette_score(X_scaled, km.labels_))\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0].plot(k_range, inertias, 'bo-', linewidth=2, markersize=8)\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel('Number of Clusters (K)')\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel('Inertia (WCSS)')\n",
    "axes[0].set_title('Elbow Method')\n",
    "axes[0].grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1].plot(k_range, silhouette_scores, 'rs-', linewidth=2, markersize=8)\n",
    "best_k = list(k_range)[np.argmax(silhouette_scores)]\n",
    "axes[1].axvline(best_k, color='green', linestyle='--', label=f'Best K={best_k}')\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel('Number of Clusters (K)')\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel('Silhouette Score')\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('Silhouette Score')\n",
    "axes[1].legend()\n",
    "axes[1].grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "print(f\"Optimal K = {best_k} (highest silhouette score: {max(silhouette_scores):.3f})\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Apply K-Means with optimal K\n",
    "km_best = KMeans(n_clusters=best_k, random_state=42, n_init=10)\n",
    "df['KMeans_Cluster'] = km_best.fit_predict(X_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visualize clusters in original scale\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "colors = ['steelblue', 'coral', 'green', 'purple', 'orange']\n",
    "for i in range(best_k):\n",
    "    mask = df['KMeans_Cluster'] == i\n",
    "    ax.scatter(df[mask]['Annual_Income_k'], df[mask]['Spending_Score'],\n",
    "               c=colors[i], label=f'Cluster {i}', alpha=0.7, s=50)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Centroids in original scale\n",
    "centroids_orig = scaler.inverse_transform(km_best.cluster_centers_)\n",
    "ax.scatter(centroids_orig[:, 0], centroids_orig[:, 1],\n",
    "           c='black', marker='X', s=250, zorder=5, label='Centroids')\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Annual Income (k$)')\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Spending Score')\n",
    "ax.set_title(f'K-Means Clustering (K={best_k})')\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cluster profiles\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Cluster Profiles ===\")\n",
    "profile = df.groupby('KMeans_Cluster')[['Annual_Income_k', 'Spending_Score', 'Age']].mean().round(1)\n",
    "profile['Count'] = df.groupby('KMeans_Cluster').size()\n",
    "print(profile)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 5: Hierarchical Clustering"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.cluster import AgglomerativeClustering\n",
    "from scipy.cluster.hierarchy import dendrogram, linkage\n",
    "\n",
    "# Dendrogram (use subset for visibility)\n",
    "X_sample = X_scaled[:50]  # first 50 for dendrogram\n",
    "Z = linkage(X_sample, method='ward')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "dendrogram(Z, truncate_mode='lastp', p=20, leaf_rotation=90, leaf_font_size=8)\n",
    "plt.axhline(y=4, color='red', linestyle='--', label='Cut line (4 clusters)')\n",
    "plt.title('Hierarchical Clustering — Dendrogram (50 samples)')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Sample Index')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Distance (Ward)')\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply Agglomerative Clustering on full dataset\n",
    "agg = AgglomerativeClustering(n_clusters=best_k, linkage='ward')\n",
    "df['Hier_Cluster'] = agg.fit_predict(X_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "hier_sil = silhouette_score(X_scaled, df['Hier_Cluster'])\n",
    "km_sil = silhouette_score(X_scaled, df['KMeans_Cluster'])\n",
    "print(f\"K-Means silhouette: {km_sil:.3f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Hierarchical silhouette: {hier_sil:.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 6: DBSCAN — Noise Detection"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.cluster import DBSCAN\n",
    "\n",
    "# Try different eps values\n",
    "eps_values = [0.3, 0.5, 0.8]\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(15, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, eps in zip(axes, eps_values):\n",
    "    db = DBSCAN(eps=eps, min_samples=5)\n",
    "    labels = db.fit_predict(X_scaled)\n",
    "    n_clusters = len(set(labels)) - (1 if -1 in labels else 0)\n",
    "    n_noise = (labels == -1).sum()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    unique_labels = set(labels)\n",
    "    for lbl in unique_labels:\n",
    "        mask = labels == lbl\n",
    "        color = 'gray' if lbl == -1 else colors[lbl % len(colors)]\n",
    "        label = 'Noise' if lbl == -1 else f'Cluster {lbl}'\n",
    "        ax.scatter(X[mask, 0], X[mask, 1], c=color, label=label, alpha=0.6, s=30)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    ax.set_title(f'DBSCAN eps={eps}\\nClusters: {n_clusters}, Noise: {n_noise}')\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel('Annual Income (k$)')\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel('Spending Score')\n",
    "    ax.legend(fontsize=7)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.suptitle('DBSCAN with Different eps Values', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Section 7: Algorithm Comparison"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Final comparison\n",
    "db_best = DBSCAN(eps=0.5, min_samples=5)\n",
    "db_labels = db_best.fit_predict(X_scaled)\n",
    "n_db_clusters = len(set(db_labels)) - (1 if -1 in db_labels else 0)\n",
    "\n",
    "if n_db_clusters > 1:\n",
    "    # Only compute silhouette for non-noise points\n",
    "    mask_valid = db_labels != -1\n",
    "    db_sil = silhouette_score(X_scaled[mask_valid], db_labels[mask_valid]) if mask_valid.sum() > 1 else 0\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    db_sil = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Algorithm Comparison ===\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'Algorithm':<25} {'Clusters':>10} {'Silhouette':>12} {'Notes'}\")\n",
    "print('-' * 65)\n",
    "print(f\"{'K-Means':<25} {best_k:>10} {km_sil:>12.3f} {'Needs K specified'}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'Hierarchical':<25} {best_k:>10} {hier_sil:>12.3f} {'Dendrogram shows structure'}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'DBSCAN (eps=0.5)':<25} {n_db_clusters:>10} {db_sil:>12.3f} {'Finds noise points'}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Business Insight from K-Means Clusters ===\")\n",
    "segment_names = {}\n",
    "for i, row in profile.iterrows():\n",
    "    inc = row['Annual_Income_k']\n",
    "    spd = row['Spending_Score']\n",
    "    if inc > 70 and spd > 60:\n",
    "        segment_names[i] = 'Premium Customers (High Income, High Spend)'\n",
    "    elif inc > 70 and spd < 40:\n",
    "        segment_names[i] = 'Careful Spenders (High Income, Low Spend)'\n",
    "    elif inc < 45 and spd > 55:\n",
    "        segment_names[i] = 'Budget-Stretch (Low Income, High Spend)'\n",
    "    elif inc < 45 and spd < 50:\n",
    "        segment_names[i] = 'Budget Conscious (Low Income, Low Spend)'\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        segment_names[i] = 'Average Customers (Mid segment)'\n",
    "\n",
    "for cid, name in segment_names.items():\n",
    "    cnt = profile.loc[cid, 'Count']\n",
    "    print(f\"  Cluster {cid}: {name} — {cnt} customers\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
